   "evidence": "The file's only criteria are global sections, affine opens, residue field, ringChar, Spec and the Nonempty hom; none is stalk-level. Repo practice is to use `@[expose]` on `Prop` defs that downstream files must unfold (grep: 19 `@[expose] def \u2026 : Prop` declarations across 14 files).",
   "file": "TauCeti/AlgebraicGeometry/Scheme/CoefficientInvertibility.lean",
   "fix": "Add `theorem isInvertibleOn_iff_forall_isUnit_stalk : X.IsInvertibleOn n \u2194 \u2200 x : X, IsUnit (n : X.presheaf.stalk x) := Iff.rfl` and an elimination lemma `IsInvertibleOn.isUnit_stalk (h : X.IsInvertibleOn n) (x : X) : IsUnit (n : X.presheaf.stalk x)`. Keep the body unexposed.",
   "issue": "`IsInvertibleOn` is a public `def` without `@[expose]`, and there is no lemma stating its defining property (`\u2200 x, IsUnit (n : X.presheaf.stalk x)`). In-file proofs use `intro x`/`unfold`; downstream files cannot, and can only reach stalk invertibility indirectly through `isInvertibleOn_iff_isUnit` and a germ map.",
   "line": 42
  }
 ],
